{
 "item": "HOLD",
 "capturedAt": "2026-11-04",
 "question": "Where does a held block sit, and does the window width decide the center line on phones?",
 "how": "real mouse in headless Chrome on an empty not-linked page, with one new blank section and new Shape blocks, nothing saved: Exit Without Saving after each run. Desktop frame 1600 wide, row pitch 41.09, column pitch 58.79. Phone frame 428 wide, 10 tracks, column pitch 48.45. bx and by are the block's distance from where it started.",
 "start": "a press does nothing. A move past 10px starts the drag but changes nothing: no ring, no transform. The next move shows it. A release right after that one move is no drag: one move of 200, 100 and a release left the area as it was.",
 "follows": "inside the limits the block is at the pointer on both axes, moving down, up, left and right, and at the same place coming back. Holding still changes nothing (1.5s waits).",
 "limits": {
  "top": "the top of the grid box",
  "bottom": "the bottom of the grid box, which grows with the target in the same move: bottom gap 0",
  "left": "the left of the grid box, within 0.33px",
  "right": "4px short of the grid box: the block's right edge stops at 1596 of 1600 and at 423.67 of 428. Why 4 is not known, it is what both views measure",
  "target": "the limits hold the block only. The target and the ring still follow the pointer"
 },
 "grid": "the grid has max(its own rows, last row of the target) rows while held, going down and coming back up: 8 rows, 11 at target 6 / 2 / 12 / 8, 13 at 8 / 2 / 14 / 8, 9 at 4 / 2 / 10 / 8, 8 at 1 / 2 / 7 / 8",
 "width": "a lone held block has the width of its target. It takes a margin track when the target does: 341.75 becomes 382.95 at 1 / 21 / 7 / 27 and at 1 / 1 / 7 / 7. Wider, its left edge stays where it was. Narrower, its center stays where it was: from 1 / 1 / 7 / 7 at dx 80 the block is at 100.55 and not 80. A group keeps its widths.",
 "target": "the step rule is G4's, in SNAP.json. These sweeps agree with it: sideways it stays to dx 34 and moves at 35, then at 94; coming back the same; down it stays to 26 and moves at 27, then at 68. Full width 1 / 2 / 7 / 26 stays to dx 50 and goes to 1 / 3 / 7 / 27 at dx 60; on phones full width goes between dx 12 and 16 on both sides. The limits below do not stop the target. One exception to the edge in front, from one sweep: a block on the left margin track going right goes by its left edge: 1 / 1 / 7 / 7 stays at dx 40, 1 / 2 / 7 / 8 at dx 80 and 120, 1 / 19 / 7 / 25 at dx 1100.",
 "group": "both blocks get the same transform. It has the pressed block's limits: left stops at -100 as for a lone block, the bottom too. The other block is not held inside the grid: at dx 1000 its right edge is 2029. The ring stops when the box reaches the side: 1 / 11 / 7 / 27. Only the pressed block on the left was measured, so a group pressed on its right block is not known.",
 "centerLine": {
  "window": "the window width does not decide it. Mobile View holds at windows 1600, 1000, 800 and 500 (a window asked to be 428 came out 500) gave the same 17 readings: the frame is 428 wide in all of them",
  "phones": "phones have the line, in the same place and colors, but only while it is yellow: no dashed line, at any point in 3 sweeps. The earlier single hold at a 428 window was away from the center",
  "rule": "a lone held block: yellow when the center of the block at its own width is within half a column of the canvas center, on desktop and on phones. Not the target: full width stays on the centered target 1 / 2 / 7 / 26 to dx 50, but is dashed from dx 30, and on phones 1 / 3 / 7 / 11 is yellow to 23.67 off the center. A resize goes by the target: east -24 yellow at 1 / 2 / 7 / 10, east -36 none at 1 / 2 / 7 / 9.",
  "snap": "phones also center-snap: a 7 column block takes one more column within half a column of the center, as 1 / 2 / 7 / 10, at width 376"
 },
 "notMeasured": "a group on phones. The rule for the 4px",
